<title>USA: Caraustar says 1997 starting slowly.</title>
<headline>Caraustar says 1997 starting slowly.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caraustar Industries Inc said Tuesday that while 1997 was starting slowly and might not outperform the 1996 first half, the company's goal is to make 1997 another record year for sales and earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;The expectation is for a stronger finish for the current year,&quot; said Tom Brown, president and chief executive officer of the producer of recycled paperboard.  </p>
<p>The company today reported fourth-quarter net sales rose to $159.6 million from $136.6 million a year ago. Net income per share rose to $2.28 from $1.66.</p>
</text>
